---
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy | Papa Bravo"
  description="How Papa Bravo AB handles personal data on papabravo.se. No advertising or analytics cookies are used."
  path="/privacy"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Section narrow>
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      {site.legalName} is responsible for this website. The site is built to work without tracking.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site does not do</h2>
    <p>
      There is no advertising, no analytics product and no marketing cookie. Meta Pixel, Google
      Analytics, Google Tag Manager and similar tools are not loaded. Because of that, the site
      does not ask you to accept cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>If you get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Email, phone and LinkedIn are ordinary contact channels. The form on the contact page does
      not send your message to a server run by Papa Bravo. It opens your own email app, addressed
      to {site.email}, so you can send it yourself. What you write is then handled as email between
      you and Papa Bravo.
    </p>
    <p>
      That correspondence is used to reply and, if it becomes an assignment, to carry out the work
      you asked about. It is not used for a newsletter, and it is not sold.
    </p>

    <h2>Server logs</h2>
    <p>
      When the site is hosted, the web server may keep standard technical logs, such as IP address,
      time and the page requested, for security and operations. How long those logs are kept
      depends on the hosting setup and should be confirmed before go-live.
    </p>

    <h2>Who to contact</h2>
    <p>
      {site.legalName}, org. no. {site.orgNumber}, {site.location}.<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      This page describes how the website behaves. It is not a complete legal privacy notice and
      should be reviewed before the site replaces papabravo.se in production.
    </p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
